Purpose: This diagram illustrates how different users and system components communicate with each other to complete specific operations.

Participants:
Participant	Responsibility
Admin	Adds and registers student details
Student	Views courses, enrolls in courses and views attendance
Teacher	Marks student attendance
Smart Campus Interface	Receives user requests and displays results
Application Controller	Processes requests and handles business logic
PostgreSQL Database	Stores and retrieves system information

Main processes illustrated:

1. Student Registration: Admin submits student details. The system sends registration information to the controller, which stores the data in the PostgreSQL database and returns confirmation.

2. Course Enrollment: Students view available courses and submit enrollment requests. The system checks enrollment status and saves the enrollment if the student is not already enrolled.

3. Attendance Management: Teachers mark student attendance. The application processes the request and saves attendance records in the database.

4. View Attendance: Students request their attendance information. The system retrieves attendance records and displays an attendance report.

Important UML element: The alt combined fragment represents alternative conditions:
- [Not Already Enrolled]: The system saves the enrollment.
- [Already Enrolled]: The system displays an already-enrolled message.
